==Solo strategy==
This strategy allows upwards of 10 points, split between elemental and catalytic, with a [[colossal pouch]] at 85+ [[runecraft]], and slightly less for other set-ups.

This strategy creates one singular barrier in the middle (between the fire and blood portals), which causes all the abyssal creatures to target it; interestingly, they do not path around the barrier, except in exceedingly rare circumstances. This makes it much simpler to run cells to upgrade the barrier and keep it recharged, allowing for relatively relaxed games. Creating more barriers near the middle will cause the run to be more difficult, as it's harder to create higher tier barriers and easier for the abyssal creatures to destroy one of the barriers, causing the Great Guardian to be damaged.

During the duration of the minigame, both guardian slots should be filled with strong (green) or overcharged (red) guardians. Creating weak (white) or medium (blue) guardians is not advised, and should only be done if there are no guardians (or only the starting weak guardian after the first two altars).

Lastly, when The Great Guardian's power reaches 60%, an explosion occurs which causes 50 damage to the barrier. Interestingly, by having the right-most barrier active with a 20 HP weak barrier (this does not apply to the left-most barrier), this damage is reduced to 19, which makes the transition into this phase much easier if a cell is not available to recharge the barrier immediately. As such, this barrier is created early into the game, and then not recharged or upgraded at all, as the barrier having more HP causes the explosion to do more damage, as the explosion appears to deal 50 damage or the right-most barrier's current health minus 1, whichever is lower. It is not targetted by abyssal creatures and poses no extra risk.
